" Docker Architecture "
--------------------
Docker Client ---> is responsible for to interacting user to docker daemon by using docker commands 
Docker Daemon ---> it is a heart of docker it manages all docker components -- images, containers, networking, volumes, compose, swarm 
Docker Registry ---> it will store all public and private images

user ---> by docker commands ---> docker client --- > docker daemon ---> docker registry 

Docker --- Docker engine --- Containers --- Image --- Dockerfile --- registry 

" OS - Level - Virtualization" ---> vm -- docker install - permission to exceute-- group and user add-- run containers --- install all -- take back by image --- by Docker Commit ""
docker commit cont1 mahi-img:v1 --- with the new image we can get all installed files in new container by running with this image 

Dockerfile -- text file -- contains instructions to create a image -- based on application dependencies + libraries -- dev+ DevOps -- will create a dockerfile

Dockerfile components
FROM ---> taking from any base image instead of zero 
RUN ---> for executing the commands
CMD ---> same but while container runtime it will exceute
COPY ---> copying the local files to inside the container
ADD ---> any internet links i will copy to inside the container 
WORKDIR ---> it will create a folder and places
LABEL ---> it will tell the information of the image owner
ENV ---> by this we can set the variables insise the container
ENTRYPOINT ---> high preference to run the commands --- can't overide
EXPOSE ---> port number expose 
ARGS ---> it will give the outside container variables














